{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdPYfHQfAsiT5oyFKb95K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YYxftwPuSGPTxDhMPeAtzx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/arena-ws.Mdeg1r/SOLUTION.md","content":"# Solution\n\nTwo bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:\n\n1. **`get` didn't refresh recency.** A successful lookup returned the value but never\n   moved the key to the MRU end of the `OrderedDict`, so a recently-read key could\n   still be picked as the eviction victim. Fixed by calling `move_to_end(key)` before\n   returning.\n\n2. **`put` evicted on updates.** The capacity check ran unconditionally, so overwriting\n   an *existing* key (which doesn't grow the cache) still popped the LRU entry, silently\n   dropping an unrelated key. Fixed by only evicting when the key is new\n   (`key not in self._data and len(...) >= capacity`).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":160,"cache_read_input_tokens":22658,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":160,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":73,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa59abd5-771b-4c71-971e-66a222a4764b","uuid":"7fccda2c-ee8e-48d8-aa94-46d208a8fc92","timestamp":"2026-07-25T22:14:49.677Z","request_id":"req_011CdPYfGFDNF9b11gWJpbUZ"}
